ulation utilities in Release 08.1. Continuing through the release mappings for the remaining utilities, tracking which version each tool was introduced in through Release 15.0.\n\nLooking at the requirement states more carefully now—I need to figure out which release actually has all its dependencies ready. The code status shows Release 05.4 is only partially complete with some hash functions implemented and others not started, and checking the requirement states, only sha512sum appears listed there. This suggests sha1sum's requirements might already be handled differently, perhaps already in progress or complete.\n\nThe recent commit history shows sha256sum was actively being worked on just now, so the generation is currently tackling that task. To apply the release-driven priority rule properly, I should identify the earliest incomplete release where the requirements are marked as ready, then focus there—and Release 05.4 with srd033-sha512sum looks like the candidate, assuming its requirements R1.1 through R1.4 are actually ready. Looking at the recent task patterns, I can see that sha256sum tasks have been grouping requirements in sets of about 4, with Task 5311 covering R2.1 through R3.1 and Task 5312 handling R3.2 through R4.3. Since I don't have direct access to the weights in requirements.yaml, I'll need to make reasonable assumptions based on the constraint that each task shouldn't exceed weight 4, and the apparent structure suggests R1.x was completed earlier while R2.x through R4.x cover check mode, BSD tag format, and error handling respectively.\n\nFor sha512sum, which follows the same structural pattern as sha256sum, I should apply the same decomposition strategy—splitting the requirements into similar groupings that respect the weight budget and maintain consistency across the checksum utilities that all share the hashutil protocol. sum, I should follow the same pattern—R1.x was likely completed earlier, so I'm looking at a 3-task split starting with c