point for the ln implementation.\n\nNow I'm thinking through what the stitch agent needs to reference for this task. It'll need the SRD file itself, the hashutil package since sha512sum depends on it, and an existing similar command implementation to use as a pattern. I should point the agent toward the SRD at docs/specs/software-requirements/srd033-sha512sum.yaml, the pkg/hashutil/ directory, and maybe cmd/sha256sum/ or cmd/md5sum/ as reference implementations. For the actual files to create, I'm looking at cmd/sha512sum/main.go and the test file, though I need to check whether the project wants tests split out separately based on the P2 requirement.\n\nLooking back at how sha256sum was structured, the implementation tasks included differential testing requirements as part of the acceptance criteria, so I should probably follow that same pattern rather than splitting tests into a completely separate task.\n\nNow I'm laying out the actual task breakdown. I'll structure sha512sum into three tasks covering the core hashing functionality, then the check mode and formatting features, and finally completion with differential testing. Then I'm starting on the ln command with its basic functionality requirements.\n\nLet me verify the weight distribution across these tasks to make sure they're balanced.\n\nBased on the sha256sum pattern and GNU sha512sum behavior, I'm mapping out what each requirement likely covers: basic file hashing with the two-space format, stdin handling, binary mode flags, and signal handling for the first group. Then check mode with checksum file parsing, and the remaining requirements for completion and differential testing.\n\nFor ln, I'm outlining the core functionality: hard links as default, symbolic links with the -s flag, target directory handling, and standard signal/help flag support.\n\nNow I need to finalize the task breakdown. I'm checking the title format from recent commits—it should be \"[stitch] cmd/<name> <description> (srd<NNN> R<list>)\"—and organizing the work into four tasks: basic hashing operations, check mode with tag format support, remaining hash features, and the ln command basics. I'm also mapping out the dependencies between tasks.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":53878,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":53878},"output_tokens":33,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9cf47d83-9eb2-48a4-920e-f7443f253a45","uuid":"502b62c5-ea25-4d33-8b4f-5da0b84beac7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Dp5bvmsmN9EiBgGrEPvJsC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** GNU coreutils have no formal specs. This project derives specifications from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew GNU binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (one package per utility), `pkg/testutils` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format` (output formatting), `pkg/hashutil` (shared checksum protocol).\n\n**Current state:** 33 releases specified (00.0–15.0). Many utilities implemented. Generation run 44 is active — sha256sum just completed (commits show tasks 5311, 5312).\n\n**Next priority:** Release 05.4 is partially complete (md5sum, sha256sum done; sha512sum has all requirements \"ready\"; sha1sum not ready). After 05.4, release 06.0 (mkdir, rmdir, mktemp, ln, unlink) is next.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\n1. **srd033-sha512sum** (Release 05.4) — earliest release with ready requirements. 12 requirements, all ready. Follows identical protocol to sha256sum via pkg/hashutil. 3 tasks.\n2. **srd037-ln** (Release 06.0) — first alphabetical cmd/ package in next release. 1 task to start.\n\n## Weight Budgets\n\n```\nTask 0: srd033 R1.1(w=1) + R1.2(w=1) + R1.3(w=1) + R1.4(w=1) = 4 ✓\nTask 1: srd033 R2.1(w=1) + R2.2(w=1) + R2.3(w=1) + R3.1(w=1) = 4 ✓\nTask 2: srd033 R3.2(w=1) + R4.1(w=1) + R4.2(w=1) + R4.3(w=1) = 4 ✓\nTask 3: srd037 R1.1(w=1) + R1.2(w=1) + R1.3(w=1) + R1.4(w=1) = 4 ✓\n```\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/sha512sum basic hashing (srd033 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd033-sha512sum.yaml (full SRD for sha512sum)\n      - pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go (shared checksum protocol -- HashConfig, DigestFiles, FormatGNU)\n      - cmd/sha256sum/main.go (reference implementation of same protocol for SHA-256)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: sha512sum utility -- hash files and stdin, output GNU two-space format\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement file hashing: compute SHA-512 digest of one or more named files, output in GNU two-space format (digest followed by two spaces and filename)\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Hash stdin when no file arguments are given or when a filename argument is \\\"-\\\"\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Support binary mode flag (-b) that outputs asterisk-prefixed filename format\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Install SIGPIPE handler via sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler(), support --version and --help flags\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use pkg/hashutil.HashConfig with crypto/sha512.New and DigestLen 64\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Delegate file iteration and formatting to pkg/hashutil.DigestFiles\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Follow the exact same main() structure as cmd/sha256sum -- parse flags, build HashConfig, call DigestFiles, exit with returned code\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build -o bin/sha512sum ./cmd/sha512sum/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"echo hello | bin/sha512sum outputs correct SHA-512 digest in GNU two-space format with - as filename\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"bin/sha512sum file.txt outputs correct digest with filename\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"bin/sha512sum -b file.txt outputs asterisk-prefixed filename\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"bin/sha512sum --version prints version info and exits 0\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/sha512sum check mode and tag format (srd033 R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R3.1)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd033-sha512sum.yaml (full SRD for sha512sum)\n      - pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go (VerifyChecksums, CheckOptions, ParseChecksumLine)\n      - cmd/sha512sum/main.go (existing basic hashing implementation to extend)\n      - cmd/sha256sum/main.go (reference for check mode flag wiring)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: add --check, --warn, --quiet, --status, and --tag flags\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement check mode (-c/--check): read a checksum file, verify each entry against the filesystem, print OK or FAILED per line\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Support --warn flag that prints warnings for improperly formatted checksum lines during verification\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Support --quiet and --status flags: --quiet suppresses OK lines, --status suppresses all output and uses only exit code\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Support --tag flag that outputs BSD-style tag format: SHA512 (filename) = digest\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Delegate check mode to pkg/hashutil.VerifyChecksums with CheckOptions{Warn, Quiet, Status}\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Delegate tag format to pkg/hashutil.FormatBSDTag with algorithm string \\\"SHA512\\\"\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Follow cmd/sha256sum flag wiring pattern exactly -- same flag names, same option mapping\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build -o bin/sha512sum ./cmd/sha512sum/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"bin/sha512sum --tag file.txt outputs \\\"SHA512 (file.txt) = <digest>\\\"\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"bin/sha512sum --check checksums.txt verifies files and prints OK/FAILED\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"bin/sha512sum --check --quiet checksums.txt suppresses OK lines\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"bin/sha512sum --check --status checksums.txt exits 1 on mismatch with no output\"\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/sha512sum completion (srd033 R3.2, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3)\"\n  dependency: 1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd033-sha512sum.yaml (full SRD for sha512sum)\n      - pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go (error handling patterns in DigestFiles and VerifyChecksums)\n      - cmd/sha512sum/main.go (existing implementation to finalize)\n      - cmd/sha256sum/sha256sum_test.go (reference for differential test structure)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests, BuildBinary)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: finalize text mode flag and error handling\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests against gsha512sum\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Support text mode flag (-t) as the default mode indicator -- text mode uses two-space separator without asterisk\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Handle errors for missing or unreadable files: print diagnostic to stderr, continue processing remaining files, exit non-zero\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Exit code semantics: 0 on success, 1 when check mode finds mismatches, non-zero for I/O errors\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement differential tests using testutils.RunDiffTests comparing output against gsha512sum reference binary\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use testutils.BuildBinary(t, \\\".\\\") and exec.LookPath(\\\"gsha512sum\\\") with t.Skip if reference not found\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Test cases cover: single file, multiple files, stdin, binary mode, tag mode, check mode, missing file errors\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Set LC_ALL=C in test environment via DiffTest.Env field\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build -o bin/sha512sum ./cmd/sha512sum/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/sha512sum/... -count=1 passes (or skips if gsha512sum not in PATH)\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"bin/sha512sum nonexistent.txt prints error to stderr and exits non-zero\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"bin/sha512sum file1.txt nonexistent.txt file2.txt processes all files, prints error for missing, exits non-zero\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Differential tests cover at least 8 scenarios matching gsha512sum behavior\"\n\n- index: 3\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/ln basic hard and symbolic links (srd037 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd037-ln.yaml (full SRD for ln)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler pattern)\n      - cmd/mkdir/main.go (reference for simple file operation utility structure, if it exists; otherwise use cmd/basename/main.go)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ln/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: ln utility -- create hard and symbolic links\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Create hard links by default: ln TARGET LINK_NAME creates a hard link LINK_NAME pointing to TARGET\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Create symbolic links with -s flag: ln -s TARGET LINK_NAME creates a symbolic link\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Support target directory form: when last argument is a directory, create links inside it using target basenames\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Install SIGPIPE handler via sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler(), support --version and --help flags\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use os.Link for hard links and os.Symlink for symbolic links\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Detect target directory: if last argument is a directory (os.Stat + IsDir), create links inside u